# Update rollback
1. Confirm Boot error
2. Safe Mode + recovery media (up-to-date ISO)
3. From recovery use offline DISM to reverse pending actions or remove updates
4. Use DISM and SFC to repair corruption
5. If repairs were unsuccessful or exceed the recovery window -> restore from known good backup/snapshot

diskpart
list volume
exit

-Undo failed or looped update with offline DISM:
DISM /image:D:\ /Cleanup-Image /RevertPendingActions

-When specific update is responsible:
DISM /image:D:\ /Get-Packages /Format:Table
Inspect suspected package:
DISM /image:D:\ /Get-PackageInfo /PackageName:"exact_package_ID"
Then remove identified package:
DISM /image:D:\ /Remove-Package /PackageName:"exact_package_ID"

-Repair Windows files or the component store if necessary:
DISM /image:D:\ /Cleanup-Image /RestoreHealth
(add updated /Source iso if needed)
sfc /scannow /offbootdir=D:\ /offwindir=D:\Windows

-If update from /Source:
DISM /Get-ImageInfo /ImageFile:E:\sources\install.wim
The output identifies the image indexes and Windows editions. Select the image corresponding to your installed server rather than assuming an index.

Assuming your index is "2":
DISM /Image:D:\ /Cleanup-Image /RestoreHealth /Source:WIM:E:\sources\install.wim:2

-When server boots up after being fixed:
DISM /Online /Cleanup-Image /restoreHealth
sfc /scannow
